<title>JAPAN: Japan June rubber imports down 6.97 pct yr/yr-MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan June rubber imports down 6.97 pct yr/yr-MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's rubber imports in June totalled 45,996 tonnes, down 6.97 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday showed. Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			June 97	 May 97     June 96</p>
<p> Total		45,996	 47,191	49,443</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand	   31,751	 36,162	33,726</p>
<p> Indonesia	  10,685	  8,721	12,870</p>
<p> Malaysia	    2,916	  1,250	 1,976</p>
<p>Total imports in the first six months of 1997 were 351,373 tonnes against 340,532 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
